{title: Drift}
{artist: Melic}
{key: D}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Sing it low, sing it [G]slow,
[D]Carry it [A7]home,
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Watch the last light [G]leave the [D]fire,
[D]Bones of something [G]like a [D]pterodactyl,
[D]Fences running [G]down to [D]wire,
[D]Every branch of [G]it a [D]fractal,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Morning water [A]running [D]cold,
[D]Every willow [A]turning brown and [D]gold,
[D]Windows in the [A]rain,
[D]Furrows lying [A]bare and [D]plain,
{end_of_verse}

{x_melic_scheme: ABAB}
{start_of_bridge}
[A]Hold it while the [E]room is [A]bright,
[A]Sing it once a[E]gain to[A]night,
[A]Let the whole of [E]it go [A]now,
[A]Sing it out again and [E]hold it up until it lands some[A]how,
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Sing it low, sing it [G]slow,
[D]Carry it all the long way [A7]home,
{end_of_chorus}
